IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 1220 of 2021
CITATION: (2021) 19 SCC 41
YEAR: 2021

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: U.U. Lalit, Ajay Rastogi, Aniruddha Bose

PARTIES:
Newtech Promoters vs State of UP

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 3 RERA, Section 18 RERA, Section 40 RERA

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
retroactive application of rera, homebuyers refund, ongoing projects, recovery of interest

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Affirmed that RERA applies retroactively to ongoing real estate projects initiated before the Act, protecting homebuyers' statutory rights to refunds with interest.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 3 RERA, Section 18 RERA, Section 40 RERA.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

